nodecode-sgme is a rewrite of freehul's freehul/sgme:

  https://github.com/freehul/sgme
  commit f12c9bfa2cc9f4a59420376cb91176abb882948b
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 freehul (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is adapters/hermes of that commit. Its tools keep their
names, their parameters and the endpoints they ask: sgme_memory_search,
sgme_conversation_search and sgme_skill_search on POST /v1/search with their
scopes; sgme_answer on POST /v1/answer; sgme_inject on POST /v1/inject;
sgme_wiki_search and sgme_wiki_pages on GET /v1/wiki/search and
GET /v1/wiki/pages; sgme_skill_get and sgme_skill_list on GET /v1/skills;
sgme_signal_pull, sgme_signal_claim and sgme_signal_ack on
GET /v1/events/pull and POST /v1/admin/care/signals/<id>/{consume,ack};
sgme_health on GET /v1/health; sgme_stats on GET /v1/admin/stats. The
X-API-Key header, the agent/admin key split, the loopback default at
http://127.0.0.1:9910, the default search scopes (memory and skills), the
# user / # assistant text of an appended turn, the asynchronous refinement
trigger, the profile block composed from the server's title and items, and
the role prompt's place above it are the original's too.

What was left out, and why: the ~44-tool surface is carried as the fourteen
a session actually reaches for; the original's roles, credentials, three
pools (ideas, demands, projects), skill and wiki writes, config and refine
administration, and its credential vault tool (off by default there) are
reached from the SGME server's own console instead. The profile block rides
Nodecode's :round point as a system-reminder rather than a provider's static
system prompt, because that is the seam this harness has, and a turn's
append is queued to a worker instead of a thread per call. LICENSE is the
repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
